this is the site where a Yeti Airlines  flight carrying 72 people crashed in The  Nepalese tourist town of Pokhara  a search and Recovery team worked  through the day Monday to retrieve  bodies from deep within a narrow Gorge  the plane took off from Kathmandu less  than an hour later it came down near its  destination the newly opened Pokhara  International Airport it narrowly missed  homes on either side of the city Gorge  and river which runs through the town  it's tragic that we lost 72 people  aboard the plane but if it had crashed a  couple of meters on either side we would  have lost many more an army and police  recovery team has worked to retrieve  bodies and identified personal  belongings found in the wreckage  the plane was carrying 57 Nepalese and  15 foreign Nationals flying in Nepal is  challenging as the country is surrounded  by mountains and difficult Terrain in  the past the country has witnessed  numerous crashes early in the day a  search and Recovery team retrieved the  black box of the ill-fated Yeti Airlines  flight experts hope it will provide  answers to the tragedy tensions Run High  as families and relatives outside a  hospital wait to claim their loved ones  the brother-in-law of this Indian  businessman was on the plane Sanjay  jaiswal had traveled to the town to see  his older sister who had just had a baby  we'd like to do the last ride soon but  there was a lot of process and red tape  involved it's frustrating I'm waiting  hospital staff try to placate distressed  family members but they'll have to wait  at least another day before they can lay  their loved ones to rest ramyata limbu  Al Jazeera in Pokhara Nepal
 

